IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`

-- g6-art18-governor-duties.l4: Article 18 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, General duties of governors of registered charities.
-- Inputs from other groups (PLAN section (c)): IP6 `the entity is a registered charity` (G1); IP5 `the entity` (G1); IP12 the conduct is misconduct
-- within Article 2(10) (G1), carried here as a field of the record of a governor's conduct, one per governor (see the integrator note in FRAGMENT-G6.md).
-- Output to other groups: IP14, `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` (G8 reads it as `the governor has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)`).
-- A duty is a regulative rule typed by the role that acts and what is done; "good faith", "due diligence", "a prudent person", "ought to have become aware"
-- and "a reasonable time" are determinations, so each is a fact the caller supplies; none is computed.
-- The duties of Article 18(1) and (2) state no period, so they carry no WITHIN: a trace leaves them standing until the act is done.

§ `Part 5 -- Governors of registered charities`

§§ `Article 18 -- General duties of governors of registered charities`

-- What a governor does under Article 18, in the value-actor style: the first actor field of each act is its performer (doc/concepts/legal-modeling/actors-and-actions).
DECLARE `Act under Article 18` IS ONE OF
    `seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently with its registered purposes and statement`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `seek in good faith to ensure the charity complies with every direction, requirement, notice and duty imposed on it by or under the Law`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `act with due diligence`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `act as would a prudent person`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `act to the best of the governor's ability and skill`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `observe the utmost good faith`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`

-- What Article 18(4) asks about each governor of a charity. One record per governor, and the list of them is the charity's board; the governor's name
-- is the identity by which "another governor" is found (phrasebook 6.6: equality of the identifying field is identity).
-- Every field is a witness-level fact or a determination the caller supplies; the field named for Article 2(10) is IP12 applied to this governor's own conduct.
DECLARE `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` HAS
    name IS A STRING
        @desc The governor's name; it identifies the governor among the governors of the charity
    `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether this governor's own conduct contravenes a provision or is an offence mentioned in Article 2(10); the answer of Article 2(10) for that conduct
    `concurs in the misconduct of the charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity (Article 18(4)(b))
    `assists or encourages these other governors to engage in misconduct` IS A LIST OF STRING
        @desc The names of the other governors whom this governor assists or encourages to engage in misconduct (Article 18(4)(c)); empty if none
    `becomes aware or ought to have become aware of misconduct, or of the intention of another governor to engage in it` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 18(4)(d)(i): whether the governor becomes aware, or ought to have become aware, of any misconduct in relation to the charity or of another governor's intention to engage in misconduct
    `actively conceals that misconduct or that intention` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 18(4)(d)(ii), first limb: whether the governor actively conceals the misconduct or the intention
    `continues the concealment beyond a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the concealment lasts longer than a reasonable time (read only under the reading that the reasonable time qualifies the concealment too)
    `fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 18(4)(d)(ii), second limb: whether the governor fails, within a reasonable time, to take proper steps to protect or restore the charity's property or to prevent the misconduct

§§§ `Article 18(1) -- the governor's duty to seek, in good faith, to ensure what the charity does`

-- src:465 | (1) A governor of a registered charity must seek, in good faith, to ensure that the charity –
-- src:466 | (a) acts in a manner that is consistent with its registered charitable purposes and with its registered public benefit statement; and
@ref Article 18(1)(a) (src:465-466)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(1)(a) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently with its registered purposes and statement` MEANS
    PARTY `a governor`
    MUST  `seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently with its registered purposes and statement` `a governor`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:465 | (1) A governor of a registered charity must seek, in good faith, to ensure that the charity –
-- src:467 | (b) complies with any direction, requirement, notice or duty imposed on it by or under this Law.
@ref Article 18(1)(b) (src:465) (src:467)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(1)(b) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity complies with the Law` MEANS
    PARTY `a governor`
    MUST  `seek in good faith to ensure the charity complies with every direction, requirement, notice and duty imposed on it by or under the Law` `a governor`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- "A governor of a registered charity must seek ... that the charity (a) ... and (b) ...": both limbs, so the two duties run together (RAND).
-- The duty is the governor's of a REGISTERED charity, so it arises only where the entity is one (IP6).
-- src:465 | (1) A governor of a registered charity must seek, in good faith, to ensure that the charity –
-- src:466 | (a) acts in a manner that is consistent with its registered charitable purposes and with its registered public benefit statement; and
-- src:467 | (b) complies with any direction, requirement, notice or duty imposed on it by or under this Law.
@ref Article 18(1) (src:465-467)
@export Whether a governor of the entity owes the Article 18(1) duty to seek, in good faith, to ensure that the charity acts consistently with its registered purposes and statement and complies with the Law; returns the duty (a deontic value) for a governor of a registered charity, or nothing owed where the entity is not a registered charity
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(1) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently` `the entity is a registered charity` MEANS
    IF   `the entity is a registered charity`
    THEN `Art 18(1)(a) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity acts consistently with its registered purposes and statement`
         RAND
         `Art 18(1)(b) the governor must seek in good faith to ensure the charity complies with the Law`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 18(2) -- the standard of care of a governor of an unincorporated body`

-- F6.7: which governors paragraph (2) binds. The words are "A governor of a registered charity, that is an unincorporated body or association of persons
-- falling within Article 2(1)(i)": taken literally, the relative clause qualifies the charity, so only governors of such bodies. The other reading binds every governor.
-- "Article 2(1)(i)" is the unincorporated-body kind of entity; a charity falls within it if its `kinds of entity` include that kind (the narrower "relevant
-- unincorporated entity" of Article 2(8) is used only in the definition of governor and is not what paragraph (2) says).
@ref Article 18(2) (F6.7) (src:468)
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.7 reading A: the standard of care binds only the governors of unincorporated bodies within Article 2(1)(i)` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity` MEANS
        `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND elem `an unincorporated body or association of persons` (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`)

@ref Article 18(2) (F6.7) (src:468)
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.7 reading B: the standard of care binds every governor of a registered charity` `the entity is a registered charity` MEANS
    `the entity is a registered charity`

-- src:468 | (2) A governor of a registered charity, that is an unincorporated body or association of persons falling within Article 2(1)(i), must in the execution of his or her duties and in the exercise of his or her powers and discretions –
@ref Article 18(2) (src:468)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `which governors Article 18(2) binds`
    WHEN `only the governors of unincorporated bodies within Article 2(1)(i)`
        THEN `F6.7 reading A: the standard of care binds only the governors of unincorporated bodies within Article 2(1)(i)` `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity`
    WHEN `every governor of a registered charity`
        THEN `F6.7 reading B: the standard of care binds every governor of a registered charity` `the entity is a registered charity`

-- src:469 | (a) act –
-- src:470 | (i) with due diligence,
-- src:471 | (ii) as would a prudent person,
-- src:472 | (iii) to the best of the governor’s ability and skill; and
@ref Article 18(2)(a) (src:469-472)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(2)(a) the governor must act with due diligence, as would a prudent person and to the best of the governor's ability and skill` MEANS
        `Art 18(2)(a)(i) the governor must act with due diligence`
    RAND `Art 18(2)(a)(ii) the governor must act as would a prudent person`
    RAND `Art 18(2)(a)(iii) the governor must act to the best of the governor's ability and skill`

-- src:470 | (i) with due diligence,
@ref Article 18(2)(a)(i) (src:470)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(2)(a)(i) the governor must act with due diligence` MEANS
    PARTY `a governor`
    MUST  `act with due diligence` `a governor`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:471 | (ii) as would a prudent person,
@ref Article 18(2)(a)(ii) (src:471)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(2)(a)(ii) the governor must act as would a prudent person` MEANS
    PARTY `a governor`
    MUST  `act as would a prudent person` `a governor`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:472 | (iii) to the best of the governor’s ability and skill; and
@ref Article 18(2)(a)(iii) (src:472)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(2)(a)(iii) the governor must act to the best of the governor's ability and skill` MEANS
    PARTY `a governor`
    MUST  `act to the best of the governor's ability and skill` `a governor`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:473 | (b) observe the utmost good faith.
@ref Article 18(2)(b) (src:473)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(2)(b) the governor must observe the utmost good faith` MEANS
    PARTY `a governor`
    MUST  `observe the utmost good faith` `a governor`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:468 | (2) A governor of a registered charity, that is an unincorporated body or association of persons falling within Article 2(1)(i), must in the execution of his or her duties and in the exercise of his or her powers and discretions –
-- src:469 | (a) act –
-- src:470 | (i) with due diligence,
-- src:471 | (ii) as would a prudent person,
-- src:472 | (iii) to the best of the governor’s ability and skill; and
-- src:473 | (b) observe the utmost good faith.
@ref Article 18(2) (src:468-473)
@export Whether and how a governor of the entity must act with due diligence, as would a prudent person, to the best of the governor's ability and skill, and in the utmost good faith (Article 18(2)); returns the duty for a governor the paragraph binds, on the reading given, or nothing owed
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The reading of Article 18(2) to apply: only governors of unincorporated bodies within Article 2(1)(i) (default), or every governor of a registered charity
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
        @desc The entity, with its kinds of entity under Article 2(1)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 18`
`Art 18(2) the governor must act with due diligence and in utmost good faith` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity` MEANS
    IF   `Art 18(2) the governor is bound by the standard of care` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity`
    THEN `Art 18(2)(a) the governor must act with due diligence, as would a prudent person and to the best of the governor's ability and skill`
         RAND
         `Art 18(2)(b) the governor must observe the utmost good faith`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 18(3) -- the duties apply despite the constitution`

-- "The duties imposed by this Article apply despite any contrary provision in the constitution or the constitutional Law of the charity, except to any extent
-- that such provision imposes a more onerous duty." Whether a provision is contrary to a duty, and whether it is more onerous, are judgements of the caller.
-- The answer is whether the duty of this Article prevails over the provision (TRUE), or the provision stands because it asks more of the governor (FALSE).
-- src:474 | (3) The duties imposed by this Article apply despite any contrary provision in the constitution or the constitutional Law of the charity, except to any extent that such provision imposes a more onerous duty.
@ref Article 18(3) (src:474)
@export Whether a provision of a charity's constitution or constitutional Law is overridden by the duties of Article 18 (it is contrary to them and does not impose a more onerous duty)
GIVEN `the provision is contrary to a duty imposed by this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the provision of the constitution or the constitutional Law is contrary to a duty under Article 18
      `the provision imposes a more onerous duty` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether, to the extent in question, the provision imposes a more onerous duty than Article 18 does
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(3) the provision of the constitution is overridden by the duties of this Article` `the provision is contrary to a duty imposed by this Article` `the provision imposes a more onerous duty` MEANS
        `the provision is contrary to a duty imposed by this Article`
    AND NOT `the provision imposes a more onerous duty`

§§§ `Article 18(4) -- when a governor engages in misconduct`

-- The four cases are a list of ways in, joined by "or". Cases (b), (c) and (d) look at the governor's own conduct, the charity's, and the other governors',
-- so "misconduct" of a governor is a recursion through case (c): B misconducts by assisting A who misconducts; C by assisting B. Cases (a), (b) and (d) are
-- the base; case (c) steps to another governor one level down. The recursion is bounded by the number of governors (a chain through n governors takes
-- at most n steps, and a cycle of assisting governors with no base misconduct among them proves nothing, which is the least fixed point).
-- src:476 | (a) the governor contravenes a provision, or commits an offence, mentioned in Article 2(10);
@ref Article 18(4)(a) (src:476)
GIVEN `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4)(a) the governor contravenes a provision, or commits an offence, mentioned in Article 2(10)` `the governor` MEANS
    `the governor`'s `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`

-- src:477 | (b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity;
@ref Article 18(4)(b) (src:477)
GIVEN `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4)(b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity` `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governor` MEANS
        `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)`
    AND `the governor`'s `concurs in the misconduct of the charity`

-- src:480 | (i) becomes aware or ought to have become aware of any misconduct in relation to the charity, or of the intention of another governor to engage in misconduct, and
@ref Article 18(4)(d)(i) (src:480)
GIVEN `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4)(d)(i) the governor becomes aware or ought to have become aware of misconduct, or of the intention of another governor to engage in it` `the governor` MEANS
    `the governor`'s `becomes aware or ought to have become aware of misconduct, or of the intention of another governor to engage in it`

-- F6.8: what "within a reasonable time" qualifies. The sentence is "actively conceals that misconduct or that intention, or fails within a reasonable time to
-- take proper steps": the words sit inside the second limb and the comma before "or" suggests they do not reach back to the first.
@ref Article 18(4)(d)(ii) (F6.8) (src:481)
GIVEN `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.8 reading A: the reasonable time qualifies only the failure to take proper steps` `the governor` MEANS
        `the governor`'s `actively conceals that misconduct or that intention`
    OR  `the governor`'s `fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct`

@ref Article 18(4)(d)(ii) (F6.8) (src:481)
GIVEN `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.8 reading B: the reasonable time qualifies both the concealment and the failure to take proper steps` `the governor` MEANS
        (    `the governor`'s `actively conceals that misconduct or that intention`
         AND `the governor`'s `continues the concealment beyond a reasonable time`)
    OR  `the governor`'s `fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct`

-- src:481 | (ii) the governor actively conceals that misconduct or that intention, or fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct.
@ref Article 18(4)(d)(ii) (src:481)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4)(d)(ii) the governor conceals the misconduct, or fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps` interp `the governor` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `what the reasonable time of Article 18(4)(d)(ii) qualifies`
    WHEN `the reasonable time qualifies only the failure to take proper steps`
        THEN `F6.8 reading A: the reasonable time qualifies only the failure to take proper steps` `the governor`
    WHEN `the reasonable time qualifies both the concealment and the failure to take proper steps`
        THEN `F6.8 reading B: the reasonable time qualifies both the concealment and the failure to take proper steps` `the governor`

-- src:479 | (d) the governor –
-- src:480 | (i) becomes aware or ought to have become aware of any misconduct in relation to the charity, or of the intention of another governor to engage in misconduct, and
-- src:481 | (ii) the governor actively conceals that misconduct or that intention, or fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct.
@ref Article 18(4)(d) (src:479-481)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` interp `the governor` MEANS
        "(d) the governor –"
    ... "(i)" ... `Art 18(4)(d)(i) the governor becomes aware or ought to have become aware of misconduct, or of the intention of another governor to engage in it` `the governor`
    AND "(ii)" ... `Art 18(4)(d)(ii) the governor conceals the misconduct, or fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps` interp `the governor`

-- "Another governor": a governor of the charity with a different name from this one, whom this governor assists or encourages.
@ref Article 18(4)(c) (src:478)
GIVEN `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
      `the other` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4)(c) the governor assists or encourages the other governor to engage in misconduct` `the governor` `the other` MEANS
        NOT (`the other`'s name EQUALS `the governor`'s name)
    AND elem (`the other`'s name) (`the governor`'s `assists or encourages these other governors to engage in misconduct`)

-- F6.24: does assisting or encouraging another governor to engage in misconduct need that governor to have engaged in it? The words are "assists or encourages
-- another governor to engage in misconduct": "to engage in" can be read as the purpose of the help (so the help is misconduct whatever came of it) or as
-- the thing helped (so there is misconduct to help). The survey's reading, which is taken, makes the other governor's misconduct a condition. It follows that
-- misconduct is computed to a depth: at depth 0 case (c) cannot step, and at depth n case (c) steps to a governor's misconduct at depth n MINUS 1.
@ref Article 18(4)(c) (F6.24) (src:478)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the governors of the charity` IS A LIST OF `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.24 reading A: the assisting or encouraging is misconduct only if the other governor engages in misconduct, to depth` interp `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governors of the charity` n `the governor` MEANS
        n GREATER THAN 0
    AND any (GIVEN other YIELD
                    `Art 18(4)(c) the governor assists or encourages the other governor to engage in misconduct` `the governor` other
                AND `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct to depth` interp `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governors of the charity` (n MINUS 1) other)
            `the governors of the charity`

@ref Article 18(4)(c) (F6.24) (src:478)
GIVEN `the governors of the charity` IS A LIST OF `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
      `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.24 reading B: the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct` `the governors of the charity` `the governor` MEANS
    any (GIVEN other YIELD
            `Art 18(4)(c) the governor assists or encourages the other governor to engage in misconduct` `the governor` other)
        `the governors of the charity`

-- src:478 | (c) the governor assists or encourages another governor to engage in misconduct; or
@ref Article 18(4)(c) (src:478)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the governors of the charity` IS A LIST OF `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4)(c) the governor assists or encourages another governor to engage in misconduct, to depth` interp `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governors of the charity` n `the governor` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether assisting another governor is misconduct only if that governor engages in misconduct`
    WHEN `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct only if the other governor engages in misconduct`
        THEN `F6.24 reading A: the assisting or encouraging is misconduct only if the other governor engages in misconduct, to depth` interp `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governors of the charity` n `the governor`
    WHEN `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct`
        THEN `F6.24 reading B: the assisting or encouraging is misconduct whether or not the other governor engages in misconduct` `the governors of the charity` `the governor`

-- src:475 | (4) For the purposes of this Law a governor engages in misconduct if –
-- src:476 | (a) the governor contravenes a provision, or commits an offence, mentioned in Article 2(10);
-- src:477 | (b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity;
-- src:478 | (c) the governor assists or encourages another governor to engage in misconduct; or
-- src:479 | (d) the governor –
-- src:480 | (i) becomes aware or ought to have become aware of any misconduct in relation to the charity, or of the intention of another governor to engage in misconduct, and
-- src:481 | (ii) the governor actively conceals that misconduct or that intention, or fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct.
@ref Article 18(4) (src:475-481)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the governors of the charity` IS A LIST OF `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct to depth` interp `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governors of the charity` n `the governor` MEANS
        "For the purposes of this Law a governor engages in misconduct if –"
    ..  "(a)" ... `Art 18(4)(a) the governor contravenes a provision, or commits an offence, mentioned in Article 2(10)` `the governor`
    ..  "(b)" ... `Art 18(4)(b) the governor concurs in misconduct by the charity` `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governor`
    ..  "(c)" ... `Art 18(4)(c) the governor assists or encourages another governor to engage in misconduct, to depth` interp `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governors of the charity` n `the governor`
    OR  "(d)" ... `Art 18(4)(d) the governor becomes aware of misconduct and conceals it or fails to act` interp `the governor`

-- The depth that suffices is the number of governors: a chain of assisting governors cannot be longer than the board, and a cycle adds no governor.
-- src:475 | (4) For the purposes of this Law a governor engages in misconduct if –
@ref Article 18(4) (src:475)
@export Whether a governor of a registered charity engages in misconduct under Article 18(4): by a breach or offence within Article 2(10), by concurring in the charity's misconduct, by assisting or encouraging another governor who engages in misconduct, or by concealing misconduct or failing to act on it; the answer is IP14
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here Article 18(4)(c) and (d)(ii) (default: the other governor's misconduct is needed, and the reasonable time qualifies only the failure to act)
      `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the charity's own conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)
      `the governors of the charity` IS A LIST OF `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
        @desc One record of conduct for every governor of the charity, including the governor in question
      `the governor` IS A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
        @desc The conduct of the governor in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct` interp `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governors of the charity` `the governor` MEANS
    `Art 18(4) the governor engages in misconduct to depth` interp `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the governors of the charity` (count `the governors of the charity`) `the governor`
